  \tab    Several examples of specific file editing and transmitting\par
 \tab    the updated file to the SIMH simulator are provided.\par
 \tab    Additionally, a series of commands is provided to implement\par
\tab    generic file processing requiring no changes to the Command\par
\tab    window.\page\tab d) The general icon color scheme chosen includes specific colors\par
\tab    for related functions as well as colors associated with two of\par
\tab    the supported operating systems [OS/8 and P?S/8 configured\par
\tab    without limitations].  These color cues assist the user in\par
\tab    selecting the desired function.  Advanced users can modify any\par
\tab    of these considerations; however, beginners are advised to\par
\tab    work with the standard release as documented here.\par
